    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my 2018 civic is making this really loud, high pitched squealing noise whenever i step on the gas to accelerate. i think it might be a belt issue? can u explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why a bad one would make that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt is a crucial drive belt that transfers power from the engine's belt drive to various accessories, like the alternator, power steering pump, and A/C compressor. When this belt wears out or starts to slip, the friction generated causes a high-pitched squealing noise, especially under load like when accelerating. This noise indicates that the belt is not gripping the pulleys correctly and needs to be inspected or replaced promptly to prevent further damage.",
