    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i was looking at mine and it looks pretty cracked/frayed in some spots. if i don't change it right away is it gonna just snap, or could it cause other things to fail? also, sometimes it just happens for no reason, like it'll squeal for a second then stop completely. is that normal or is something else going on?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A cracked or frayed serpentine belt is a serious issue as it is very likely to snap, which will immediately stop essential systems like charging your battery or powering your water pump. Intermittent squealing, where it happens and stops, often suggests the belt is overly loose, has worn pulleys, or that an accessory component is slightly binding or failing intermittently. You should have a mechanic inspect not only the belt but also the tensioners and the pulleys themselves to diagnose the cause accurately.",
      "source": "target",
